    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0641" n="547" xml:id="pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/376: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kornfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-03T15:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 3—2:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>47. Referring to Legation’s no. 46, June 30. Representative of Sinclair has
                    refused to give engagement asked for by Persian Government. Accordingly the oil
                    commissioners have stricken out article 25 of contract (Legation’s no.
                        343)<anchor n="9" xml:id="d475-f1"/> which denies validity of any other
                    grants, and they have adopted instead article 29 of bill which affirms only that
                    no other grant has been confirmed by Mejliss.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kornfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
